{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 27, :comments ["<b>And he burned on it incense of spices</b> — Moses burned on it [the incense] all seven days of the ordination. And even though it was not stated in the command (Exodus 40:5) \"and you shall burn on it incense of spices,\" he [Moses] understood this from all the other services, for He commanded him here (Exodus 40:4) that he arrange the bread and kindle the lamps. And likewise, \"and he offered on it the burnt-offering and the meal-offering\" (Exodus 40:29) — Moses is the one who offered, for so he was commanded (Exodus 29:38), \"And this is what you shall do upon the altar,\" that he [Moses] should begin to do so himself during the days of ordination, for all the commands there (from verse 1 onward) concern the service of Moses. And afterward He said (Exodus 40:42 [29]), \"a perpetual burnt-offering throughout your generations,\" that the priests should do so for all generations. Therefore it states in the section of Pinchas (Numbers 28:6), \"a perpetual burnt-offering that was made at Mount Sinai\" — that Moses began it there.\n\nAnd behold, Moses our Rabbi in all the services is the first High Priest, and therefore he also burned the incense. And perhaps it is included in \"and you shall place the golden altar for incense\" (Exodus 40:5) — that you should burn incense on it immediately. And what it says in the command (above 30:6–7), \"and you shall place it before the curtain, and Aaron shall burn on it incense of spices\" — this is to instruct concerning its matter from the day Aaron began in his priesthood and forever, for so it says (there 30:8), \"and when Aaron kindles the lamps between the evenings\" — and the matter is only from this day onward, for here (Exodus 40:4) He explicitly commanded Moses, \"and you shall kindle its lamps.\" And in the commentary of Rashi (on the verse before us) I saw: \"and Aaron burned on it incense\" — morning and evening, as it says (above 30:7–8), \"in the morning, in the morning, when he tends the lamps, etc., and when Aaron kindles the lamps between the evenings,\" etc. And I do not know whether this is a scribal error."], :book :exodus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 40, :notes {0 "The verse cited as Exodus 40:42 in the Hebrew is evidently a slip for 40:29; I have retained the reference as Ramban gives it."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:22:51.331078963Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}